  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1-sin\u2061x}{sin\u2061x},$ find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let $u=1-sin\u2061x$ and $v=sin\u2061x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-cos\u2061x\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=cos\u2061x.\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}-u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{sin\u2061x\\cdot (-cos\u2061x)-(1-sin\u2061x)\\cdot cos\u2061x}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{cos\u2061x(-sin\u2061x-1+sin\u2061x)}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{cos\u2061x\\cdot (-1)}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{sin\u2061x}\\cdot \\frac{cos\u2061x}{sin\u2061x} \\\\  & =-csc\u2061xcot\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
